WEBVTT

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:12.780
The crank pin: a cylinder 10 in diameter and 25 long, with an M3 threaded hole in one end; it fits into the crank

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:27.721
Centre on the origin, diameter 10: fully constrained. Pad 25 mm

00:00:27.721 --> 00:00:39.180
A hole needs a position: click the top face, create a sketch, and put a point on the origin

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:43.185
Select that sketch and click Hole

00:00:43.185 --> 00:00:50.988
Thread type: ISO metric regular profile, size M3x0.5

00:00:50.988 --> 00:00:56.429
Hole type: the second item, the tap drill—drill now, tap later, no thread geometry

00:00:56.429 --> 00:01:04.980
Depth 7.5; untick the drill point angle so the bottom is flat

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:14.780
It is a threaded hole, but the thread isn't modelled: it is cut at the tap-drill size 2.5 and remembers "M3"—drawings label the thread automatically

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:24.640
Pad adds material, Pocket removes it; Hole is a specialised pocket: threads, counterbores and drill points are all options
